starting_money: "3d6x100"
extraction_notes: |
  - Underseas, printed 111-112. The New Navy''s shipboard trooper, and the only
    class in this book with a Military Occupational Specialty.
  - ITS MOS IS A CHOICE INSIDE A CHOICE, which is why it is modelled with choice
    groups rather than flat skill lists. Every other MOS in this catalog grants
    every skill under the chosen option; this one names five to eight skills per
    specialty, marks them major or minor, and has the player take ONE major at
    +15% and THREE minors at +10%. An MOS option''s `skills` takes the same shape
    as `occ_skills`, choice groups included, so the pair of groups is the
    faithful reading.
  - THE MEDICAL SPECIALTY IS TWO OPTIONS, NOT ONE, because the book offers a
    genuine either/or with different shapes. Medical Doctor is a "special"
    major that includes all its required skills, gets NO specialty bonus, and
    grants NO minor selections at all; the general medical route is an ordinary
    one-major-three-minors. Splitting them is the only way to make both
    expressible, and a single option could not have held either faithfully.
  - THE BOOK CONTRADICTS ITSELF ON THE MINOR COUNT within one paragraph -
    "three minor ones" and then "the two minor skills" on printed 111. The
    O.C.C. skill list on printed 112 reads "Minor Skill Specialty (3; +10%)".
    Three is stored: two statements to one, and the skill list is the more
    precise of the three.
  - THREE RELATED-SKILL CATEGORIES ARE GATED ON THE SPECIALTY and are stored
    NARROW. Espionage: None unless Special Forces. Rogue: None unless a SEAL.
    Wilderness: land navigation and carpentry only unless a SEAL. There is no
    key for "this category opens if you chose that MOS", so the stored version
    is the one that applies to seven of the nine specialty options, and the
    widening is in the restrictions where a SEAL player will read it. Storing
    the WIDE version would have handed every artilleryman and cook the
    espionage list.
  - TWO SPECIALTIES GRANT A FREE HAND TO HAND UPGRADE and it is stored inside
    the option rather than on the class: Special Forces gets martial arts,
    Underwater Specialist gets expert, and the other seven keep the class''s
    Basic. Because an MOS APPENDS to occ_skills rather than replacing them, a
    SEAL character carries both Basic and the upgrade; the upgrade''s note says
    which one governs.
  - "ANY W.P. (MINOR)" ON THE MILITARY POLICE OPTION IS NOT STORED. A choice
    group takes either a `from` list or a `categories` list, and that option''s
    minors already need a `from` list for the four named rows. The allowance is
    in the group''s note.
  - NO `sdc_base` AND NO `mdc_base`, so it needs a `CORE_SDC_BY_CLASS` entry.
    3D6: every Navy member is trained in combat, the class grants three W.P.s
    outright and Military is open, and printed 111 is explicit that there are no
    rear echelons on Rifts Earth.
---

# Navy Seaman

## Lore

The crews of the USS Ticonderoga and her associated vessels combine the skills of a Navy trooper with a technical or scientific specialty. Thanks to the computerised systems that survived the Great Cataclysm, they are among the best educated humans on Rifts Earth - 100% literate, and technically skilled with it.

Every Navy member is trained in combat, even though most operations are run by the Marines. The reason is simple enough: on Rifts Earth there are no rear echelons. A monster can appear on the bridge of a ship as easily as it can hit troops on a front line, and the Ticonderoga''s expeditions have more than once been settled by hand to hand fighting aboard ship.

## GM Notes

Most seamen - or women; there is no gender bias in the New Navy - fill one or more functions aboard ship, from communications and maintenance to flying a carrier-based fighter. Decide the character''s area of specialty at creation and assign one major specialty skill and three minor ones.

Two of the nine specialty options are SEAL programs, and they change the class considerably: a SEAL may take Espionage, Rogue and Wilderness skills that are otherwise closed to a seaman, and gets a free hand to hand upgrade on top.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'navy-seaman');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'navy-seaman';
SELECT count(*) AS stub_gear FROM gear WHERE slug IN ('navy-body-armor', 'm-2011-pistol', 'luggage');

